{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmOnCut","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmOnCut","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmDeriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrability.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrability.LogMeromorphic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmBoundary","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ConstantOffOnePoint"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.continuousWithinAt_clog_one_sub_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.continuousWithinAt_clog_one_sub_mul","kind":"theorem","line":749,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L749-L769","doc":"**`w ↦ log(1 − w·t)` is continuous at a cut crossing, restricted to\n`Im w ≤ 0`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.re_inversion_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.re_inversion_identity","kind":"theorem","line":677,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L677-L727","doc":"**The inversion identity, `x ≥ 1`.**\n\n    Re cLiTwoExt(x) + Re cLiTwoExt(1/x) + ½·log²x = π²/3\n\n`G' = 0` on `(1,∞)` (`hasDerivAt_inversionCombo`), `G` is continuous up to and\nincluding the branch point, and `G(1) = 2·Re cLiTwoExt(1) = π²/3`\n(`re_cLiTwoExt_one`). The exceptional point `x = 1`, where the derivative does\nnot exist, costs nothing — `constant_of_hasDerivWithinAt_zero_off_point` is\nbuilt for exactly that. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.re_cLiTwoExt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.re_cLiTwoExt_one","kind":"theorem","line":673,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L673-L675","doc":"`Re cLiTwoExt(1) = π²/6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.continuousOn_cLiTwoExt_ofReal_Icc'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.continuousOn_cLiTwoExt_ofReal_Icc'","kind":"theorem","line":654,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L654-L671","doc":"Continuity of `cLiTwoExt` along `[0,b]` for **any** `b > 0` — the primitive\nargument again, now that integrability holds on `0..b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_one","kind":"theorem","line":613,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L613-L650","doc":"**`cLiTwoExt 1 = π²/6`.** Both `cLiTwoExt` and `cLiTwo` are continuous along\n`[0,1]` and agree on `[0,1)`; the value at the branch point follows.\n\n⚠ Neither `cLiTwoExt_eq_cLiTwo` (needs `‖y‖ < 1`) nor\n`cLiTwoExt_eq_cLiTwo_of_norm_le_one` (needs `y ∈ notCut`) reaches `1` — it is\nexactly the excluded point of both. The continuity above is what closes the gap,\nand it exists only because step (1) supplied integrability at `x = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.continuousOn_cLiTwoExt_ofReal_Icc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.continuousOn_cLiTwoExt_ofReal_Icc","kind":"theorem","line":590,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L590-L611","doc":"**`cLiTwoExt` is continuous along `[0,1]`, up to and including the branch\npoint.** Because it is a primitive of an integrable function — integrability at\n`x = 1` being step (1) with `x = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_ofReal_eq_primitive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_ofReal_eq_primitive","kind":"theorem","line":582,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L582-L588","doc":"`cLiTwoExt` along the reals **is** the primitive of the `y = 1` kernel.\nHolds at `0` too, where both sides are `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwo_one","kind":"theorem","line":569,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L569-L580","doc":"`cLiTwo 1 = π²/6` — the series converges *at* `1`, so this is immediate from\n`hasSum_one_div_succ_sq`; no boundary theory is involved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_inversionCombo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_inversionCombo","kind":"theorem","line":522,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L522-L565","doc":"**The inversion combination is locally constant on `(1,∞)`.**\n\n    G(x) := Re cLiTwoExt(x) + Re cLiTwoExt(1/x) + ½·log²x\n\nhas `G' = 0`. The three derivatives are `−log(x−1)/x`, `(log(x−1) − log x)/x` and\n`log x / x`, and they cancel identically. Route 35 G3 measures `G ≡ π²/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_re_cLiTwoExt_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_re_cLiTwoExt_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":507,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L507-L520","doc":"`d/dx Re cLiTwoExt(x) = −log|1−x|/x`, real `x > 0`, `x ≠ 1`. `Real.log` is\neven, so this reads `−log(x−1)/x` on `x > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cLiTwoExt_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cLiTwoExt_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":496,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L496-L503","doc":"**`d/dx cLiTwoExt(x) = −log(1−x)/x` for real `x > 0`, `x ≠ 1` — including on\nthe cut.** Ray direction `1`, so the radial parameter *is* `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cLiTwoExt_radial_ofReal'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cLiTwoExt_radial_ofReal'","kind":"theorem","line":469,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L469-L494","doc":"The radial derivative with the right-endpoint cap removed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_clog_one_sub_div_ofReal'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_clog_one_sub_div_ofReal'","kind":"theorem","line":438,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L438-L467","doc":"Integrability on `0..b` for any `b > 0`, not just `b = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cLiTwoExt_radial_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cLiTwoExt_radial_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L384-L428","doc":"**The radial derivative, generalised to real `x > 0` — including on the cut.**\n\n`hasDerivAt_cLiTwoExt_radial` requires `y ∈ notCut`, which real `x > 1` fails.\nThat hypothesis was doing three jobs: integrability on `[0,t]`, continuity of the\nkernel at `t`, and measurability near `t`. All three now hold for real `x`\nwithout it — the first by `intervalIntegrable_clog_one_sub_div_ofReal`, the other\ntwo by `continuousAt_liTwoKernel_ofReal`.\n\n⚠ `hxt : 1 − x·t ≠ 0` is **load-bearing and replaces `notCut`**: at `t = 1/x` the\nkernel genuinely diverges. The original excluded that point implicitly via\n`slitPlane`; a version admitting it would be false. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.continuousAt_liTwoKernel_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.continuousAt_liTwoKernel_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L359-L382","doc":"**The kernel is continuous at real `u`, on the cut**, provided only\n`u ≠ 0` and `1 − x·u ≠ 0`. No `slitPlane` hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.continuousAt_arg_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.continuousAt_arg_step","kind":"theorem","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L343-L357","doc":"The `arg` step is **locally constant** away from the sign change. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_clog_one_sub_div_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_clog_one_sub_div_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L323-L330","doc":"**`cLiTwoExt`'s integrand is integrable at real `x > 0`** — both\nsingularities handled: the logarithmic one at `t = 1/x` (if it is in range) and\nthe removable one at `t = 0`. This is `qou-invr` step (1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_integrand_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_integrand_left","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L284-L321","doc":"**Near `0` the integrand is integrable**, by rescaling to the existing\n`slitPlane` lemma. With `c = 1/(2x)` the substitution `t = c·u` turns the\nintegrand into `log(1 − u/2)/u`, whose slit hypothesis holds outright. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_integrand_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_integrand_right","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L267-L281","doc":"**Away from `0` the integrand is integrable**: `1/t` is continuous there, so\nit peels off against `intervalIntegrable_clog_one_sub_mul`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_clog_one_sub_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_clog_one_sub_mul","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L240-L263","doc":"**`t ↦ Complex.log (1 − x·t)` is interval-integrable on any interval**, for\nreal `x` — across the cut, singularity and branch jump included. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_arg_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_arg_step","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L226-L238","doc":"The bounded `arg` half: a two-valued step function is interval-integrable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_real_log_one_sub_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_real_log_one_sub_mul","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L212-L224","doc":"**`t ↦ Real.log (1 − x·t)` is interval-integrable on ANY interval**, the\nlogarithmic singularity at `t = 1/x` included.\n\nVia `intervalIntegrable_log_norm_meromorphicOn`: `1 − x·t` is affine, hence\nanalytic, hence meromorphic, and `Real.log` is even so `‖·‖` costs nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.arg_one_sub_mul_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.arg_one_sub_mul_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L205-L210","doc":"`arg (1 − x·t)` for real `x, t` is an explicit two-valued step function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.abs_im_log_ofReal_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.abs_im_log_ofReal_le","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L196-L201","doc":"And the imaginary part is bounded by `π`, uniformly — the half that is\nintegrable for trivial reasons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.re_log_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.re_log_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L190-L194","doc":"The real part is a genuine real logarithm — and `Real.log` is even, so the\nabsolute value costs nothing. This is the form `intervalIntegrable_log'`\nconsumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.log_ofReal_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.log_ofReal_eq","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmOnCut.lean#L178-L188","doc":"**The real-argument decomposition of the principal logarithm.**\n\nFor real `r`, `log r = log |r| + arg(r)·I`, with `arg(r) ∈ {0, π}` according to\nthe sign. Separating the divergent real part from the bounded `arg` is the first\nstep of every route to integrability on the cut. ","signatureChunk":0}]}